        hardEdges: ["Don't say stuff is bad. Zeno said it's indifferent — it can be used well or badly. A toy isn't bad. Lying to get it is.", "Don't skip the counterexample: health is good, right? Zeno said no — health can make you cruel if you use it to bully. Only how you choose can't be misused."],
        reading: [{ heading: "What is truly good?", body: "Zeno asked a big question: what is truly good? Not what feels good. Not what you want. What is good no matter what? He said: being kind. Being brave. Being fair. Being honest. These are good because you choose them, and nobody can make you use them badly. A toy can be shared or grabbed. A cookie can be a gift or a bribe. But kindness is always kind. That's what 'good' means for Zeno: the choice you make that can't go wrong." }],
