        reading: [{ heading: "The hardest claim", body: "Zeno's founding axiom: virtue is the only good. Everything else — health, wealth, reputation, pleasure, even life — is indifferent. Not worthless. Indifferent. Capable of being used well or badly. A strong body can protect or bully. A good grade can inspire or inflate. Wealth can feed or corrupt. Only virtue — the rational choice to act wisely, justly, courageously, moderately — cannot be misused, because virtue IS the disposition to use everything well. This is why Zeno said it's the only good. Not the highest good among many. The only one. The pushback is obvious and fair: so health doesn't matter? Of course it matters. It's just not what makes you good." }],
